From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: crypto: sun8i-ce - Add HMAC-SHA1 and HMAC-SHA256 for the H616

The H616 crypto engine computes HMAC-SHA1 (algorithm 0x16) and
HMAC-SHA256 (0x17) itself. Register hmac(sha1) and hmac(sha256) for the
H616, with the library implementations as fallback.

One HMAC is one task marked as the last package (common control bit
15): the engine pads the data itself. The ctr address points to the key
(K1), one block long: a longer key is hashed first and a shorter one
padded with zeroes, as HMAC does. The engine uses that key only for the
outer hash; it does not put the key XOR ipad block in front of the data
(the vendor driver, which passes the bare message, gets wrong MACs), so
the driver keeps that block next to the key and makes it the first
source SG. The key address points to the length in bits of the whole
inner input (ipad block and message), and the data length is the same
number of bits. The source is read in words; the last word may be a
partial one.

Only digest() runs on the engine; init/update/final/finup, export and
import, the empty message, more than 7 message SGs, unaligned SGs and
SGs that are not a whole number of words before the last one go to the
fallback.

Like the engine's other new modes, both register below every CPU
implementation (the library ones use the CPU's SHA instructions): the
CPU stays the default and the engine is used when it is asked for by
driver name (hmac-sha1-sun8i-ce, hmac-sha256-sun8i-ce). The other
variants get CE_ID_NOTSUPP for both.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
